{number: 39}
{title: There Shall Be Showers of Blessing}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] There shall be showers of blessing:
This is the [G7] promise of love;
There shall be [C] seasons refreshing,
[G7] Sent from the Savior a-[C] bove.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] Showers of blessing,
Showers of blessing we [G7] need:
[C] Mercy drops 'round us are [F] falling,
But for the [C] showers we [G7] plead. [C]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] There shall be showers of blessing
Precious re-[G7] viving again;
Over the [C] hills and the valleys,
[G7] Sound of abundance of [C] rain.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] There shall be showers of blessing;
Send them up-[G7] on us, O Lord;
Grant to us [C] now a refreshing,
[G7] Come, and now honor Thy [C] Word.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C] There shall be showers of blessing:
Oh, that to-[G7] day they might fall,
Now as to [C] God we’re confessing,
[G7] Now as on Jesus we [C] call!
{end_of_verse}
